city_le_card_pred G v hrad hnt\n199:       omega\n200:   have hrad_le := radius_le_eccentricity G v\n201:   omega\n202: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":1663,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-12T00:00:29Z","thinking":"**Understanding a Powerful Lemma**\n\nThe lemma `radius_add_one_le_of_card_compl` seems highly useful; it states that if a specific condition involving a vertex, a natural number, and the size of the graph's complement holds, then the graph's radius plus one is bounded. The key is to realize the ball expands at a minimum rate, meaning the number of uncovered vertices is an upper bound on the number of steps to reach all vertices.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"roman domination number\" \"radius\" graph theory","toolAction":"Searching literature on roman domination and radius","toolSummary":"Search web for roman domination and radius"}}]}
